.TH OTPME-CLIENT 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-client \- manage OTPme clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-client
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIclient\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-client
manages client objects in the OTPme system. Clients are connected either via RADIUS or LDAP. A special client is the OTPme SSO portal, which provides Single Sign-On for web applications. Each client is assigned an access group that controls which tokens are authorized, and can optionally have addresses, secrets, and SSO configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Client Management
.TP
.B add \fR[\fB\-\-enable\-oidc\fR] [\fB\-\-scopes\fR \fISCOPES\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-scopes\fR \fISCOPES\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-default\-scopes\fR] \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIaddress\fR]
Create a new client, optionally with an IP address. See the OIDC section below for the scope flags.
.TP
.B del \fIclient\fR
Delete a client.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIclient\fR]
Display client information. Without arguments, shows all clients.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List clients, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIclient\fR
Enable a disabled client.
.TP
.B disable \fIclient\fR
Disable a client without deleting it.
.TP
.B rename \fIclient\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a client.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIclient\fR \fIunit\fR
Move client to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIclient\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Access Group and Authorization
.TP
.B access_group \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIaccess_group\fR]
Set or display the client's access group. The access group controls which tokens are authorized to authenticate via this client.
.TP
.B add_token \fIclient\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Add a token to the client.
.TP
.B remove_token \fIclient\fR \fItoken_path\fR
Remove a token from the client.
.TP
.B list_tokens \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIclient\fR
List tokens assigned to the client. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR) and \fB\-\-token\-types\fR to filter by token type.
.TP
.B add_role \fIclient\fR \fIrole\fR
Add a role to the client.
.TP
.B remove_role \fIclient\fR \fIrole\fR
Remove a role from the client.
.TP
.B list_roles \fIclient\fR
List roles assigned to the client.
.TP
.B list_scopes \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIclient\fR
List OIDC scopes assigned to the client.
.SS dot1x
.TP
.B enable_dot1x \fIclient\fR
Enable 802.1x authentication for this client.
.TP
.B disable_dot1x \fIclient\fR
Disable 802.1x authentication for this client.
.SS Login Control
.TP
.B limit_logins \fIclient\fR
Limit logins to tokens and roles explicitly assigned to this client.
.TP
.B unlimit_logins \fIclient\fR
Allow logins from all tokens authorized by the access group.
.TP
.B secret \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIsecret\fR]
Set or change the client secret (e.g. RADIUS shared secret).
.TP
.B show_secret \fIclient\fR
Display the client secret.
.SS Address Management
.TP
.B add_address \fIclient\fR \fIaddress\fR
Add an IP address to the client.
.TP
.B del_address \fIclient\fR \fIaddress\fR
Remove an IP address from the client.
.SS Auth Cache
.TP
.B enable_auth_cache \fIclient\fR
Enable authentication caching for this client.
.TP
.B disable_auth_cache \fIclient\fR
Disable authentication caching.
.TP
.B auth_cache_timeout \fIclient\fR \fItimeout\fR
Set authentication cache timeout.
.SS SSO Configuration
.TP
.B enable_sso \fIclient\fR
Enable SSO (Single Sign-On) for this client.
.TP
.B disable_sso \fIclient\fR
Disable SSO for this client.
.TP
.B sso_name \fIclient\fR \fIname\fR
Set the SSO display name for this client.
.TP
.B sso_logo \fIclient\fR \fIimage_path\fR
Set the SSO logo image for this client.
.TP
.B dump_sso_logo \fIclient\fR
Export SSO logo as base64.
.TP
.B del_sso_logo \fIclient\fR
Delete the SSO logo.
.TP
.B login_url \fIclient\fR \fIurl\fR
Set the client login URL.
.TP
.B helper_url \fIclient\fR \fIurl\fR
Set the SSO helper URL.
.TP
.B enable_sso_popup \fIclient\fR
Enable SSO popup for this client.
.TP
.B disable_sso_popup \fIclient\fR
Disable SSO popup for this client.
.SS OIDC Relying Party Configuration
An OIDC client (Relying Party, RP) is enabled per site; see
.B enable_oidc
in
.BR otpme-site (1)
for the OP-side setup.
.TP
.B enable_oidc \fIclient\fR
Enable OIDC authentication for this client (the RP).
.TP
.B disable_oidc \fIclient\fR
Disable OIDC authentication for this client.
.TP
.B add_oidc_redirect_uri \fIclient\fR \fIuri\fR / \fBdel_oidc_redirect_uri \fIclient\fR \fIuri\fR
Add or remove an allowed OIDC redirect URI (\fBredirect_uri\fR) for the RP.
.TP
.B show_oidc_redirect_uris \fIclient\fR
List the RP's allowed redirect URIs.
.TP
.B add_oidc_logout_redirect_uri \fIclient\fR \fIuri\fR / \fBdel_oidc_logout_redirect_uri \fIclient\fR \fIuri\fR
Add or remove an allowed OIDC post-logout redirect URI.
.TP
.B show_oidc_logout_redirect_uris \fIclient\fR
List the RP's allowed post-logout redirect URIs.
.TP
.B add_oidc_grant_type \fIclient\fR \fIgrant_type\fR / \fBdel_oidc_grant_type \fIclient\fR \fIgrant_type\fR
Allow or disable an OIDC grant type (\fBauthorization_code\fR, \fBrefresh_token\fR, \fBclient_credentials\fR, \fBurn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code\fR).
.TP
.B show_oidc_grant_types \fIclient\fR
List the RP's allowed grant types.
.TP
.B add_oidc_response_type \fIclient\fR \fIresponse_type\fR / \fBdel_oidc_response_type \fIclient\fR \fIresponse_type\fR
Allow or disable an OIDC response type (\fBcode\fR).
.TP
.B show_oidc_response_types \fIclient\fR
List the RP's allowed response types.
.TP
.B oidc_auth_method \fIclient\fR \fImethod\fR
Set the token-endpoint auth method for the RP (\fBclient_secret_basic\fR, \fBclient_secret_post\fR, \fBnone\fR).
.TP
.B oidc_id_token_alg \fIclient\fR \fIalg\fR
Set the ID Token signing algorithm for the RP (\fBRS256\fR, \fBRS384\fR, \fBRS512\fR, \fBES256\fR, \fBES384\fR, \fBES512\fR, \fBEdDSA\fR).
.TP
.B oidc_subject_type \fIclient\fR \fBpublic\fR|\fBpairwise\fR
Set the OIDC subject type. With \fBpairwise\fR the RP receives a \fIsub\fR that is unique per (RP, user) pair; see
.B sso_fqdn
and the pairwise secret in
.BR otpme-site (1).
.TP
.B oidc_sector_identifier_uri \fR[\fB\-\-validate\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\fR] \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIuri\fR]
Set or clear the RP's OIDC sector identifier URI (only relevant for pairwise subjects). \fB\-\-validate\fR fetches the URI immediately and verifies every registered \fBredirect_uri\fR is listed; without it the check is deferred to sign-time. \fB\-\-clear\fR removes the URI.
.TP
.B oidc_backchannel_logout_uri \fR[\fB\-\-clear\fR] \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIuri\fR]
Set or clear the RP's OIDC back-channel logout URI (server-to-server logout notification). \fB\-\-clear\fR removes it.
.TP
.B enable_oidc_force_backchannel_logout \fIclient\fR / \fBdisable_oidc_force_backchannel_logout \fIclient\fR
Force / stop forcing OIDC back-channel logout POSTs to the RP.
.TP
.B enable_oidc_backchannel_tls_verify \fIclient\fR / \fBdisable_oidc_backchannel_tls_verify \fIclient\fR
Enable / disable TLS certificate verification for back-channel logout POSTs. Only disable for lab/dev RPs; in production pin a CA via
.B oidc_backchannel_ca_cert
instead.
.TP
.B oidc_backchannel_ca_cert \fR[\fB\-\-clear\fR] \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIca_cert_file\fR]
Pin a PEM CA bundle (read from file) used to verify the RP TLS cert on back-channel logout. Replaces the system trust store for this client. \fB\-\-clear\fR removes the pinned bundle.
.SS Object Changelog
.TP
.B changelog \fIclient\fR
Show the object's changelog (chronological list of changes with author, timestamp and optional custom text passed via \fB\-\-changelog\fR).
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIclient\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Open the given changelog entry in the editor named by \fBEDITOR\fR to edit its custom text.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIclient\fR \fIchangelog_id\fR
Remove a single entry from the object's changelog.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIclient\fR
Clear the object's entire changelog.
.SS Policy Management
.TP
.B add_policy \fIclient\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the client.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIclient\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the client.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIclient\fR
List policies attached to the client. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR) and \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to filter by policy type.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIclient\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIclient\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B show_acls \fIclient\fR
Display all ACLs for the client.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIclient\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIclient\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Configuration and Attributes
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] \fIclient\fR \fIparameter\fR \fR[\fIvalue\fR]
Set a configuration parameter. Use \fB\-d\fR to delete (reset to default) or \fB\-a\fR to append the value to a list-typed parameter.
.TP
.B show_config \fIclient\fR [\fIparameter\fR]
Show all configuration parameters.
.TP
.B get_config \fIclient\fR \fIparameter\fR
Show the value of a single configuration parameter.
.TP
.B description \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set client description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIclient\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIclient\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.TP
.B add_extension \fIclient\fR \fIextension\fR
Add an extension to the client.
.TP
.B remove_extension \fIclient\fR \fIextension\fR
Remove an extension.
.TP
.B add_attribute \fIclient\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Add an LDAP attribute.
.TP
.B del_attribute \fIclient\fR \fIattribute\fR=\fIvalue\fR
Remove an LDAP attribute.
.TP
.B add_object_class \fIclient\fR \fIclass\fR
Add an LDAP object class.
.TP
.B del_object_class \fIclient\fR \fIclass\fR
Remove an LDAP object class.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIclient\fR
Export client configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIclient\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all clients (across all units).
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-scope\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of OIDC scopes shown per client.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.TP
.B \-\-attribute \fIATTR\fR
Display specific attribute in list command.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving client.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH CONFIG PARAMETERS
Configuration parameters can be set with the \fBconfig\fR command and displayed with \fBshow_config\fR.
For a complete description of all available parameters and their applicable object types, see
.BR otpme (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Creating and Configuring Clients
.TP
.B otpme-client add radius_gw 10.0.0.1
Create client with IP address
.TP
.B otpme-client access_group radius_gw vpn
Assign access group to client
.TP
.B otpme-client secret radius_gw
Set RADIUS shared secret
.SS Managing Addresses
.TP
.B otpme-client add_address radius_gw 10.0.0.2
Add additional address
.TP
.B otpme-client del_address radius_gw 10.0.0.1
Remove address
.SS SSO Configuration
.TP
.B otpme-client enable_sso webapp
Enable SSO for web application
.TP
.B otpme-client sso_name webapp "My Application"
Set SSO display name
.TP
.B otpme-client login_url webapp https://app.example.com/login
Set login URL
.SS Login Control
.TP
.B otpme-client limit_logins radius_gw
Limit logins to explicitly assigned tokens
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
